Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 23:50:06 -0500
Subject: feat: the rail's Space dots stand two to a line (S-483)

docs/features/sidebar.md Y56, spaces B12. Past four Spaces the rail
showed the other Spaces as a column of dots 18 DIP apart under and above
the active chip, which took a lot of the rail's height. The active
Space's chip now leads the stack and the other Spaces stand as dots two
to a line under it, 4 DIP apart, in the order of the Spaces; the "+"
stays under them. Six Spaces take 98 DIP from the chip to the "+" where
they took 150.

The rail lays the stack out with a layout of its own; the open row keeps
its flex layout. A tab dragged over the grid lights the dot under the
pointer by filling its cell, so nothing moves, and the stack keeps its
lead until the drag leaves, so a switch on a rest does not move the Space
switched to from under the pointer. A dot is not dragged to a new place
in the grid; the Space menu still moves it.

Why: the owner asked for more room in the rail and chose this form from
renders (2026-11-13).
Removable when: never; Stedding's own sidebar.
